            <div xml:id="d568">

                <pb facs="0582" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00111 <hi rendition="#superscript">Lic. Wolf,
                        Rudolf/51</hi>/47: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-06T15:00:00+00:00">February 6, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 6—12:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>174. Your 64, February 5, 2 p.m. Consul at Havre reports all the planes still on
                    the dock there. The plan to ship planes on the Greek steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Katharictisa</hi> has apparently been abandoned as that
                    vessel sailed for Cardiff on February 3 without the planes. According to
                    stevedoring agents who were employed to handle the shipment Hunzedal is
                    endeavoring to arrange shipment to Marseille but French customs office at Havre
                    has received no instruction to issue permit thus far. Shall telegraph further
                    after hearing from Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
